%description:

Tcp.checksumMode:computed-ipv6 -- over IPv6, the segments carry a computed checksum, and a receiver discards a wrong one.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Checksums are declared correct rather than computed, unless
`checksumMode` is "computed" (MUST-2 asks for computed checksums; gap 2 of the TCP
evidence)".

The classes: declared ("declared", the default: the sender writes no checksum and marks the
header as correct) and computed ("computed": the sender computes the checksum of RFC 9293).
The code: Tcp::initialize() puts a TcpChecksumInsertionHook into the IPv4 and IPv6 modules
of the host for "computed"; Tcp::checkChecksum() of the receiver follows the mode that the
header carries, so the parameter of the sender decides whether a receiver can find a wrong
checksum. An invalid value fails at the @enum of the NED. The facet computed-ipv6: Tcp::initialize() puts the hook into the IPv6 module with its own
call. This test separates "computed" from "declared" over IPv6.

Host under test: host1, on IPv6 hosts (precondition); the application of host1 opens at 3 s,
after the address configuration, and sends 10000 bytes at 3.1 s to host2, which computes no
checksum of its own (the default). The tap replaces the checksum of the first data segment of
host1 with its one's complement and changes nothing else. Observation: level 1, host2 discards
the segment whose checksum the tap changed, and acknowledges all data: a receiver accepts a
computed checksum only when it is right, so each other segment of host1 carries the right
checksum.

%# parameter: Tcp.checksumMode
%# class: computed-ipv6
%# value: "computed"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.checksumMode
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpChecksumModeComputedIpv6")
        .intercept(tap("tap").filterPacket("tcp.destPort == 1000 && ipv6.payloadLength > 100B").nth(1)
                     .mutate([](Packet *frame) { corruptTcpChecksum(frame); })
                     .describe("the first data segment of host1: replace its checksum with the one's complement"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(3.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetDropped")
             .filterPacket("tcp.destPort == 1000")
             .describe("host2 discards the segment whose checksum is wrong")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.ackNo >= {isn} + 1 + 10000")
             .describe("the ACK of all data of host1")
             .within(2.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpChecksumModeComputedIpv6 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.checksumMode = "computed"    # the parameter under test
*.host*.typename = "StandardHost6"
*.configurator.typename = "Ipv6FlatNetworkConfigurator"
*.host1.app[0].tOpen = 3s
*.host1.app[0].tSend = 3.1s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpChecksumModeComputedIpv6: PASS
